  "problem": "Focused PR086 tests hardcoded the pre-PR005 current tree as historical/current truth (changed_count=2 and ResultCard.test.ts current bytes as historical). Root independently proved the adapter and actual WP11 suite pass on the composed PR086+PR005 candidate, but those three tests fail on the genuine 13-file current diff. Complete historical/current byte verification still has to hold for any valid current tree.",
  "resulting_behavior": "The named pre-PR005 fixture still asserts exactly two package transitions. Current-candidate checks independently compare every original sealed pin (path/hash/length) to actual current bytes and do not hardcode a current head or weaken to >=2/first-failure. Current-file mutation uses a task-owned TMPDIR fixture with the actual builder/validator; historical hashes come from retained proof and before/after hashes from real current files. Historical subject remains 294d8b40bb5a2dbe1f55cdfde4a60205de75ee1ffe48e0108eae69aea2db0f98. Current technical subject remains 7e355d27a6deb558b6626c486472763a7cfd61239e054d16e13256162de3829f (approval=null). Wrapper subject is now 822c69777c46a237eefb7da3e299854b1562ec1ac726ef1c9fa37add2c2530eb (approval=null) because adapter and tests changed. Prior PR086 replay/receipts remain byte-identical. Direct --validate/--issue still reject historical approval on the current subject. This is not combined PR005/PR086 acceptance or release qualification.",
